 ### Client (M12 part 2)
 
 - **Links:** `Game.link` is a `SwitchLink` around single player's `LocalCombatLink`; joining a room points it at a `NetLink`, so the hero's combat router, the game loop and the CombatView work unchanged. `NetLink` uploads the hero's full state at 20 Hz from the `Player` (position, velocity, facing, mode, flags, rope/zip anchor, wall, traversal, combat overlay, and every `PlayerEvent` since the last upload), sends intents and pings, and feeds enemy snapshots (with the hero's own combat state, SelfSnap), `ce` events and relayed hero states down. Room time comes from `ClockSync`; the render time is 0.1 s behind it.
-- **Remote heroes:** `RemotePlayer` implements `AnimSource`, so the hero's own `CharacterAnimator` poses other players from a 32-sample interpolation buffer; relayed events fire when the render time reaches their sample (lines attach and release in step with the motion); a changed teleport counter snaps. Level of detail: full animator under 60 m, every 3rd frame to 150 m, one shared instanced silhouette draw call to 500 m, then only a minimap dot; off-screen heroes skip the animator. Name tags are DOM labels (hidden past 120 m and behind walls); remote sounds fade out over 45 m.
+- **Remote heroes:** `RemotePlayer` implements `AnimSource`, so the hero's own `CharacterAnimator` poses other players from a 32-sample interpolation buffer; relayed events fire when the render time reaches their sample (lines attach and release in step with the motion); a changed teleport counter snaps. Level of detail: full animator under 60 m, every 3rd frame to 150 m, one shared instanced silhouette draw call to 500 m, then only a minimap dot; off-screen heroes skip the animator. Name tags are DOM labels (hidden past 120 m and behind walls); remote sounds (movement and, from the room's `ce` events, their strikes, hurt thuds and knockouts) fade out over 45 m. In PvP rooms the other heroes are strike targets for the click/F router (`HeroCombat.heroes`).
 - **Online rules** (`online.ts`): the room drives the hour (the local advance is off and the hour keys, T and Y show "Saat oda ile paylaşılıyor"; a clock message eases in over 2 s, or snaps past 0.05 h; the rooftop moment restores to the room's hour); pause sends `afk` while the world keeps going; a `correct` teleports the hero (no blend, camera snapped) and bumps the teleport counter; a dropped socket reconnects with the token (0.5, 1, 2, 4, 8 s), and the token is kept in `sessionStorage`; a kick or a failed reconnect leaves the room and single player carries on; no server within 4 s starts single player with a toast.
 - **Lobby** (`ui/lobby.ts`, `ui/online.css`): a screen of the UI's menu stack; names are checked with `net/names.ts` as you type (the server checks again). `?oda=CODE` opens it with the code; `?ws=` overrides the server address in development.
 
diff --git a/docs/DECISIONS.md b/docs/DECISIONS.md
index cf6fb41..fd83375 100644
--- a/docs/DECISIONS.md
+++ b/docs/DECISIONS.md
@@ -222,5 +222,6 @@ One line each: decision + why.
 - Clock sync snaps to a better estimate when it is more than 100 ms off and during the first 4 samples: a busy page's first round trip can leave the estimate a second off, which the 5 ms/s slew would take minutes to undo. Extrapolation of remote samples estimates velocity over at least 50 ms (two uploads a moment apart produced wild extrapolations).
 - The server's speed allowance counts at most 2 s since the last accepted state (`NET.maxStateGapS`): a client that goes quiet could otherwise teleport arbitrarily far.
 - Kicked or not reconnected within the backoff (0.5-8 s): the client leaves the room and single player continues where the hero is; the server cannot be reached within 4 s: single player starts with the toast.
-- PvP targeting through the left-click router (heroes as targets) is not wired yet: PvP intents work end to end (`net.spec.ts` sends them through the link), the router still picks enemies only.
+- PvP targeting: in a private PvP room the online controller hands the other heroes (posed at the render time, as the server checks reach; downed or away heroes left out) to `HeroCombat.heroes`, and the left click and F pick them with the same priorities as enemies (close range in front, crosshair cone, free-flow, then F's nearest in view), using the hero capsule (`tuning.body`). Right-button lines and E takedowns stay on enemies (the sim has no web lines on heroes). Public rooms never get hero targets.
+- Remote heroes' combat sounds come from the room's `ce` events, not their relayed `strike` events (a whiff also emits one): a landed strike by another hero plays punch, kick or the shield clang at that hero, a hit on another hero its hurt thud, its knockout the KO thud; faded over the same 45 m as the other remote sounds and panned from the camera. Enemy KOs stay with the combat HUD (any hitter).
 - Multi-page browser tests skip the final draw (`Game.drawPaused`, set only by the test API) because several SwiftShader pages on one machine made each frame take seconds, which slowed the fixed-step simulation (12 ticks per frame at most) and with it the 20 Hz upload.
